    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1676">

                <pb facs="1064" n="948" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg948"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.5.1/686.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Jefferson to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Managua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-02">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 2, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Yesterday President Díaz signed the new budget. For provisions see my September
                    10. At my request all other legislation suspended awaiting action on the Canal
                    Treaty and arrangements with bankers. <pb facs="1065" n="949" xml:id="pg949"/>
                    In my conversation yesterday with the Minister of Finance he stated that the
                    salaries unpaid and other accounts due for the last seven months amount to
                    $504,758 besides which President Díaz has personally signed drafts and notes
                    outstanding on account of the Government amounting to $200,000 more. The above
                    items seem large to me. It is difficult to get at all expenditures of
                    moneys.</p>
                <p>In view of the decrease in the customs and the internal revenue and the
                    consequent shortage of something like $50,000 monthly, I have suggested to the
                    Government officials the passage of an act immediately imposing taxes on
                    personal and real property; also a reorganization of the internal revenue
                    service. I would suggest, in the event of another loan and the issuance of more
                    money, that the above reforms be complied with and the income from the internal
                    revenue be supervised and paid through the National Bank.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jefferson</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
